# The console chords on a head under the open policy (ADR-1401 D1, D5):
# Ctrl+Super+Enter opens a console just after the one shown, Ctrl+Super+
# Backspace closes the one shown and does nothing on the last, a new console
# never takes an id given before, and the head stops at 4 consoles. Ctrl
# shows a link's address only while it is held (ADR-1002, section 4). With
# no head file vtium runs one head, named console. The guide runs in its
# first console; a console a chord opens gets a shell (guide.sh). --osd=full
# draws the line at the top of the head that names the console shown.
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=chords DEMO_ARGS='--osd=full'

title: the console chords

intro: Never press Ctrl+Super+Backspace on console 1 unless a step asks:
intro: this guide runs there. Each step brings you back to console 1.

step: This guide runs in console 1
run: echo "head $VTIUM_HEAD, console $VTIUM_CONSOLE"
expect: "head console, console 1": vtium runs one head, named console, and
expect: this guide runs in its first console.

step: A new console opens and shows
probe: focus
do: press Enter to start the probe, then press Ctrl+Super+Enter. Read the
do: new console's first line, press Ctrl+Super+Left to come back, then q.
expect: a new console shows at once: "This is console 2 of the head
expect: console" and the prompt "console-2$ ", under a top line that reads
expect: "● console · console 2 of 2" for about 3 seconds. Back here the line
expect: reads "console 1 of 2", and the probe shows FOCUS OUT, then FOCUS
expect: IN, and no other line: no chord sent this guide a key.

step: A new console opens just after the one shown
do: here, on console 1 of 2, press Ctrl+Super+Enter and read the new
do: console's first line. Then press Ctrl+Super+Right twice.
expect: the new console says "console 3" and its top line reads "console 2
expect: of 3": it opened between this guide and console 2. The first
expect: Ctrl+Super+Right shows console 2, "console 3 of 3", and the second
expect: brings you back here, "console 1 of 3".

step: Closing shows the next console, and an id is never given twice
do: press Ctrl+Super+Right to show console 3, then Ctrl+Super+Backspace.
do: Then press Ctrl+Super+Left to come back here, press Ctrl+Super+Enter,
do: read the new console's first line, and press Ctrl+Super+Left again.
expect: console 3 closes and console 2 shows at once, "console 2 of 2".
expect: The console you open after that says "console 4", not 3, and its
expect: top line reads "console 2 of 3".

step: A head stops at 4 consoles
do: here, on console 1 of 3, press Ctrl+Super+Enter, then Ctrl+Super+Left
do: to come back, then Ctrl+Super+Enter once more.
expect: the first press opens console 5, "console 2 of 4". The second
expect: opens nothing: you stay here, and a line at the top reads "No more
expect: consoles: console has 4, its most." for about 3 seconds.

step: The last console stays
probe: focus
do: press Enter to start the probe. Press Ctrl+Super+Right once, then
do: Ctrl+Super+Backspace three times, which closes consoles 5, 4 and 2 and
do: brings you back here. Then press Ctrl+Super+Backspace here, and q.
expect: each press closes the console shown and shows the next, and the
expect: third shows this probe again, "console 1 of 1", with FOCUS OUT and
expect: FOCUS IN in it. The last press closes nothing and prints no line,
expect: and the probe stays. If the guide vanishes instead, the check has
expect: failed: Ctrl-C in the desktop terminal that started the run ends it.

step: Ctrl shows a link's address only while it is held
run: printf '\e]8;;https://example.com/vtium-chords\e\\a link to hover\e]8;;\e\\\n'
do: rest the pointer on "a link to hover", hold Ctrl for a second, then
do: let go of Ctrl and keep the pointer still.
expect: the pointer over the link underlines all of it with dashes. While
expect: Ctrl is held, https://example.com/vtium-chords shows in inverted
expect: colors at the start of the bottom row. It goes the moment Ctrl is
expect: let go, with the pointer still and no other key pressed.

step: A console chord leaves no address behind
do: keep the pointer on the link. Press Ctrl+Super+Enter and let go of
do: every key; then press Ctrl+Super+Left and let go. Then press
do: Ctrl+Super+Right, then Ctrl+Super+Backspace, to close the new console.
expect: the new console shows no address. Back here the address shows
expect: while Ctrl is down and goes as soon as you let go, and the link
expect: stays underlined. The close brings you back here, "console 1 of 1".
